    "media:imagetext": "BOEING 737\nSOUTHWEST\nSAFETY\nINFORMATION\nSMOKING IS NOT PERMITTED\nON ANY SCHEDULED FLIGHT.\nEXIT SEATING\nAll seats in the overwing window row have been designated as exit seats.\nFederal Aviation Regulations require that all persons seated in a designated exit seat be willing and able to\nperform the functions shown on this card in the event of an emergency if a crewmember is not available.\nNo certificate holder may seat a person in a designated exit seat if the certificate holder determines that it is\nlikely that the person would be unable to perform one or more of the applicable functions because:\nThe person lacks sufficient mobility, strength, or dexterity in both arms and hands, and both legs:\n1. To reach upward, sideways, and downward to the location of emergency exit and exit-slide operating\nmechanisms;\n2. To grasp and push, pull, turn, or otherwise manipulate those mechanisms;\n3. To push, shove, pull, or otherwise open emergency exits;\n4. To lift out, hold, deposit on nearby seats, or maneuver over the seatbacks to the next row objects the\nsize and weight of overwing window exit doors;\n5. To remove obstructions similar in size and weight to overwing exit doors;\n6. To reach the emergency exit expeditiously;\nTo maintain balance while removing obstructions;\n8. To exit expeditiously;\n9. To stabilize an escape slide after deployment; or\n10. To assist others in getting off an escape slide;\nThe person must be at least 15 years of age or lacks the capacity to perform one or more of the functions\nwithout the assistance of an adult companion, parent, or other relative;\nThe person must have the ability to read and understand instructions related to emergency evacuation\nprovided by the certificate holder in printed, handwritten, or graphic form or the ability to understand oral crew\ncommands in the English language;\nThe person lacks sufficient visual capacity to perform one or more of the applicable functions without the\nassistance of visual aids beyond contact lenses or eyeglasses;\nThe person lacks sufficient aural capacity to hear and understand instructions shouted by crewmembers,\nwithout assistance beyond a hearing aid;\nThe person lacks the ability adequately to impart information orally to other passengers; or\n1. A condition or responsibilities, such as caring for small children, that might prevent the person from\nperforming one or more of the applicable functions; or\n2. A condition that might cause the person harm if he or she performs one or more of the applicable\nIn the event of an emergency, follow the directions and hand signals of your crew. If a crewmember is not\navailable to assist you, follow the instructions on this card and posted signs.\nAnother seat assignment is required of persons who 1) do not meet the selection criteria; 2) have a condition\nthat will prevent them from performing the functions; 3) may suffer bodily harm as a result of the functions; or 4)\ndo not wish to perform the functions.\nNotify your Flight Attendant if you have any questions or require reseating.",
